    "description": "Mixed Mineral and Sea Glass\nSpecimens and Coastal Finds\nLarge Lot, Mixed Era\nThis eclectic collection of geological specimens and maritime finds presents a diverse assortment of natural and processed decorative elements. The lot is highlighted by a substantial pink dyed agate slice and a clear quartz crystal cluster, alongside a large volume of surf-tumbled sea glass and a fossilized shark tooth. These pieces offer a mix of textures and colors suitable for display, lapidary study, or craft use.\nITEMS INCLUDED:\n1.\nAgate Slice\n- Large pink dyed agate with polished face and natural crystalline center\n2.\nQuartz Cluster\n- White to clear natural crystal grouping with multiple terminations\n3.\nFossil Shark Tooth\n- Large prehistoric tooth specimen with visible root and enamel patina\n4.\nSea Glass Collection\n- Substantial quantity of surf-tumbled glass in cobalt, teal, and white\n5.\nMineral Specimens\n- Includes pyrite cluster, desert rose gypsum, and polished agate geode sections\n6.\nAssorted Stones\n- Various small tumbled gravel, crystals, and a small glass display jar\nCondition:\nGood pre-owned condition. Mineral specimens show natural geological textures, inclusions, and minor edge wear consistent with handling. Sea glass is appropriately frosted and rounded from water exposure. The dyed agate slice features a high-polish finish on one side. Total weight of the collection is approximately 9 pounds.\nWarehouse Location: Cleveland\nDue to our lighting, white glare lines may appear on items - This is NOT damage\nIf you have any questions regarding the quality or authenticity of this item or general questions regarding and item, please click Contact Seller on the item page and send us a message. We are available to answer your questions Monday through Friday, 8 am - 3:00 pm, EST.\n* For combined shipping policy see the shipping tab.\nSome items may contain unseen flaws not noted in the description.\nSee Photos. Items sold as-is.",
